          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पावसाळी (pāvsāḷī) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from prāvṛṣakāla, \"the rainy season\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 8965). It is prāvṛṣ, \"the rains\", and kāla, \"time\". CDIAL lists Marathi pāvsāḷī."
            }
          ]
        },
